WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:01.830
- Welcome to the show.

00:00:01.830 --> 00:00:02.663
- [Markella] Thank you.

00:00:02.663 --> 00:00:03.496
- I literally feel like I know y'all

00:00:03.496 --> 00:00:05.463
but it's weird cause you're not
in costume for me right now.

00:00:05.463 --> 00:00:06.960
But, I love the show.

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:08.910
I know. Well, wait, here you go.

00:00:08.910 --> 00:00:09.900
I love the show.

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:12.360
I'm gonna just tell you in the beginning,

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:14.610
I never saw the movies
and I don't know why,

00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:16.380
'cause fairies and magic is all my thing.

00:00:16.380 --> 00:00:17.670
I don't know why I missed it.

00:00:17.670 --> 00:00:20.130
But your show, watching it,
made me want to watch them.

00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:22.500
So now my kids, we're all
watching them at home now.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:23.640
Because of this series.

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:24.960
It's so cool.

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:27.480
Did you, I don't know,
did you have any pressure?

00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:28.313
Like, feeling to,

00:00:28.313 --> 00:00:30.690
'cause Lord of the Rings
is such a huge novel.

00:00:30.690 --> 00:00:32.850
It's a huge show, it's
just a huge following.

00:00:32.850 --> 00:00:34.380
Did y'all feel any pressure?

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:36.180
- Pressure's how you make a diamond, man.

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:37.013
- [Kelly] Yeah, all right.

00:00:37.013 --> 00:00:37.920
I like that answer.

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:41.772
- Like, nobody puts as much
pressure on us as ourselves.

00:00:41.772 --> 00:00:44.100
We want it to be as good
as we know it can be

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:47.077
and show Tolkien respect,
and they always ask,

00:00:47.077 --> 00:00:48.690
"Do you feel pressure from the fans?"

00:00:48.690 --> 00:00:51.877
But, we're fans, and we're
taking good care of it.

00:00:51.877 --> 00:00:54.480
- Well, and it's interesting
how you're doing it.

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:55.680
Like it's a different time.

00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:57.300
And so that's the interesting concept.

00:00:57.300 --> 00:00:59.520
So, even if, I was telling
the audience before

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:00.353
the show started, I was like,

00:01:00.353 --> 00:01:02.850
even if you haven't seen the
movies, you're gonna love it.

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:05.564
It's such a whole new
world for people that,

00:01:05.564 --> 00:01:07.320
like I said, I didn't see the movies.

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:09.540
I'm highly invested in the characters.

00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:10.799
I'm very excited about yours.

00:01:10.799 --> 00:01:11.760
- (laughs) Thank you.

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:14.310
- I have to start with
asking you to explain those,

00:01:14.310 --> 00:01:15.360
this, to the world, though.

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:18.120
For people like me who lived under a rock,

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:18.953
and didn't know Lord the Rings.

00:01:18.953 --> 00:01:20.400
Like, what is the show?

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:21.606
What is it about?

00:01:21.606 --> 00:01:24.060
- It's obviously a fantasy show,

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:25.530
about Middle Earth.

00:01:25.530 --> 00:01:27.750
And our show takes
place thousands of years

00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:28.620
before the films,

00:01:28.620 --> 00:01:29.850
so you really don't need to know anything.

00:01:29.850 --> 00:01:30.683
- [Kelly] I know, yeah.

00:01:30.683 --> 00:01:31.650
- It's the first chapter.

00:01:31.650 --> 00:01:33.690
It's exactly where
you're supposed to start.

00:01:33.690 --> 00:01:37.560
Like, it's the quintessential
battle between good and evil,

00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:38.782
light and dark.

00:01:38.782 --> 00:01:39.945
- Hope and despair.

00:01:39.945 --> 00:01:41.137
- Yeah, hope and despair.

00:01:41.137 --> 00:01:42.590
- Hope and despair.
- Misery.

00:01:42.590 --> 00:01:43.423
- Misery. Tragedy.

00:01:43.423 --> 00:01:44.310
- And of course, we're
all from different races

00:01:44.310 --> 00:01:45.480
that are in Middle Earth.

00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:46.313
- Yeah.

00:01:46.313 --> 00:01:48.450
- Coming together, because
the minute we celebrate that,

00:01:48.450 --> 00:01:50.550
the minute we can always erase evil.

00:01:50.550 --> 00:01:51.633
- [Kelly] I love that thread, yeah.

00:01:51.633 --> 00:01:53.216
(audience clapping)

00:01:53.216 --> 00:01:54.558
It's such a beautiful thing.

00:01:54.558 --> 00:01:55.470
That's what I loved when I-

00:01:55.470 --> 00:01:57.510
and did you love like,
playing your character?

00:01:57.510 --> 00:01:59.130
You felt personally kinda connected

00:01:59.130 --> 00:02:00.000
to being able to do this, right?

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:01.290
- I felt hugely connected.

00:02:01.290 --> 00:02:03.420
I felt hugely connected
because the breakdown

00:02:03.420 --> 00:02:06.720
of the character in the
audition, is she's maternal,

00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:10.380
and she brings some joy, and you know-

00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:11.280
- [Kelly] And you sing.

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:12.180
- [Sophia] And I sing.

00:02:12.180 --> 00:02:13.290
- Yeah, you do.

00:02:13.290 --> 00:02:14.123
- And,

00:02:15.780 --> 00:02:19.080
yeah, so, for me, it just felt
like a really iconic moment.

00:02:19.080 --> 00:02:22.410
She is the first female dwarf
to have ever truly been seen

00:02:22.410 --> 00:02:24.840
within the world of
Tolkien, or this franchise.

00:02:24.840 --> 00:02:27.870
She is the first dwarf of
color to have ever been seen

00:02:27.870 --> 00:02:28.890
within this franchise.
(audience clapping)

00:02:28.890 --> 00:02:29.783
- [Kelly] Yeah.
- Thank you.

00:02:31.357 --> 00:02:34.710
And so, it felt like a moment to rise.

00:02:34.710 --> 00:02:37.470
And I was very, very pregnant
at the time of auditioning.

00:02:37.470 --> 00:02:40.026
And so yeah, it was this
it's been a whole lot.

00:02:40.026 --> 00:02:43.080
- Oh my God, I hated
working when I was pregnant.

00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:44.190
Were-

00:02:44.190 --> 00:02:46.320
- Two days away from giving
birth before I auditioned.

00:02:46.320 --> 00:02:47.153
- What?

00:02:47.153 --> 00:02:49.080
- Maybe engaged, midwives on stage.

00:02:49.080 --> 00:02:50.580
- Your diaphragm has left.

00:02:50.580 --> 00:02:51.870
- I doing the camera test like this.

00:02:51.870 --> 00:02:53.016
- Yeah.

00:02:53.016 --> 00:02:53.849
(Sophia laughs)

00:02:53.849 --> 00:02:54.682
- Wait, what about costumes?

00:02:54.682 --> 00:02:56.070
Was that an issue?

00:02:56.070 --> 00:02:58.050
- Costumes. Can I just say,

00:02:58.050 --> 00:03:01.890
the first conversation I
had with the design team.

00:03:01.890 --> 00:03:04.680
She said, "You're breastfeeding, right?

00:03:04.680 --> 00:03:05.730
What do you need?"

00:03:05.730 --> 00:03:07.477
- First of all, I love
that someone just said,

00:03:07.477 --> 00:03:08.954
"So, you're breastfeeding."

00:03:08.954 --> 00:03:10.470
- Yeah, yeah, exactly.

00:03:10.470 --> 00:03:11.640
- But that's so helpful.

00:03:11.640 --> 00:03:13.350
'Cause people don't think about that.

00:03:13.350 --> 00:03:14.970
- So, there's pictures of my costume

00:03:14.970 --> 00:03:17.580
but there's like these
stitchings on the shoulders

00:03:17.580 --> 00:03:20.617
and that was literally, in
between takes, me going-

00:03:20.617 --> 00:03:22.907
"So what is it, what are we say next?"

00:03:22.907 --> 00:03:25.380
(everybody laughing)

00:03:25.380 --> 00:03:26.520
- I love that that's kind of

00:03:26.520 --> 00:03:27.990
your character in the film too, though.

00:03:27.990 --> 00:03:28.823
- Yeah.

00:03:28.823 --> 00:03:30.120
- Like very nurturing, and funny,

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:31.998
and it just, it's a
really great character.

00:03:31.998 --> 00:03:32.831
- I appreciate it, I do.

00:03:32.831 --> 00:03:34.770
- [Kelly] I love y'all's
relationship, it's so cool.

00:03:34.770 --> 00:03:37.590
And you play, Markella, you
play, it's a Hobbit, right?

00:03:37.590 --> 00:03:38.980
But y'all say, do you say half-foot?

00:03:38.980 --> 00:03:39.813
- A Harfoot.

00:03:39.813 --> 00:03:40.749
- A Harfoot, yes.

00:03:40.749 --> 00:03:42.630
- I was like, but, it's
the Hobbit thing, right?

00:03:42.630 --> 00:03:43.463
That's what it is, right?

00:03:43.463 --> 00:03:44.760
- Yeah, so they're like, yeah, they are.

00:03:44.760 --> 00:03:46.710
So, they're like the
ancestors to the Hobbits.

00:03:46.710 --> 00:03:47.543
- [Kelly] Okay.

00:03:47.543 --> 00:03:48.510
So they're kind of, you know,

00:03:48.510 --> 00:03:50.640
they have the same feet.

00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:51.840
They have the same ears.

00:03:51.840 --> 00:03:53.700
The feet come up to like,
just above the knee.

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:54.840
They're huge flippers.

00:03:54.840 --> 00:03:56.700
And you slip all around all the time.

00:03:56.700 --> 00:03:57.810
And then you-
- [Kelly] That's helpful.

00:03:57.810 --> 00:03:59.463
- Yeah, it's great, it's really
great at 3AM in the morning.

00:03:59.463 --> 00:04:01.800
It's amazing, it's so fun.

00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:03.090
And then they,

00:04:03.090 --> 00:04:05.310
but the difference is
in their circumstance.

00:04:05.310 --> 00:04:07.103
So the Hobbits have the
Shire, and they have the home,

00:04:07.103 --> 00:04:09.660
and the Harfoots are
still trying to find that.

00:04:09.660 --> 00:04:12.060
- That scene where it all comes to life.

00:04:12.060 --> 00:04:13.530
Like, when we first introduced y'all.

00:04:13.530 --> 00:04:14.494
I love it.

00:04:14.494 --> 00:04:15.327
- I know, it's so cool.

00:04:15.327 --> 00:04:16.380
- Yeah, I was like, wait, what?

00:04:16.380 --> 00:04:17.213
It was so cool.

00:04:17.213 --> 00:04:18.046
Everything came to life.

00:04:18.046 --> 00:04:20.820
And I love your character
'cause you're so curious.

00:04:20.820 --> 00:04:22.680
And you keep talking about going beyond,

00:04:22.680 --> 00:04:23.610
like, where you're from,

00:04:23.610 --> 00:04:26.910
and it's, there's just a lot
of great themes, you know,

00:04:26.910 --> 00:04:30.030
that are applicable to
society today, as well.

00:04:30.030 --> 00:04:32.730
While you're watching
this fantastical thing.

00:04:32.730 --> 00:04:34.800
So, I love your character.

00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:35.633
It's so fun.

00:04:35.633 --> 00:04:36.630
Especially, ah, I don't wanna ruin it.

00:04:36.630 --> 00:04:39.008
But when you find something
and I was like, wait, what?

00:04:39.008 --> 00:04:39.936
(all laughing)

00:04:39.936 --> 00:04:40.769
- [Markella] I was like that as well.

00:04:40.769 --> 00:04:42.240
- I know. I was like, what just shot-?

00:04:42.240 --> 00:04:43.073
And I was like, what?

00:04:43.073 --> 00:04:44.520
And it's really well done.

00:04:44.520 --> 00:04:45.930
And you play the High King.

00:04:45.930 --> 00:04:47.040
- King of the Elves, ma'am.

00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:49.776
- Yes, did you already feel
like you were the role?

00:04:49.776 --> 00:04:51.480
- (laughing) No, no. No no.

00:04:51.480 --> 00:04:53.130
They put me in like, a gold corset

00:04:53.130 --> 00:04:55.500
and I was like, oh, I guess
I'm standing up straight.

00:04:55.500 --> 00:04:56.961
- [Kelly] Just another Tuesday.

00:04:56.961 --> 00:04:57.930
- [Benjamin] (laughing) Yeah, yeah.

00:04:57.930 --> 00:04:59.160
- I love it, though.

00:04:59.160 --> 00:05:01.830
And then all the secrecy of the characters

00:05:01.830 --> 00:05:02.663
and what's going on.

00:05:02.663 --> 00:05:05.070
I love, you need to watch this show.

00:05:05.070 --> 00:05:05.910
It's so addictive.

00:05:05.910 --> 00:05:06.743
I was so glad

00:05:06.743 --> 00:05:08.614
that I had only had two
episodes in it for this,

00:05:08.614 --> 00:05:11.448
'cause I was like, I
would've stayed up all night.

00:05:11.448 --> 00:05:12.390
(audience clapping)
Now joining us,

00:05:12.390 --> 00:05:15.060
from the Lord of the
Rings, the Rings of Power,

00:05:15.060 --> 00:05:18.510
say hello to Nazanin Boniadi, Lloyd Owen,

00:05:18.510 --> 00:05:19.710
and Ismael Cruz Cordova.

00:05:20.608 --> 00:05:21.613
(audience cheers)

00:05:21.613 --> 00:05:24.696
(upbeat funky music)

00:05:36.225 --> 00:05:37.770
- [Sophia] Look at us!

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:39.870
- I'm so, y'all, this is about to blow up.

00:05:39.870 --> 00:05:41.670
I'm just glad I'm talking
to you first, right now.

00:05:41.670 --> 00:05:43.380
'Cause I'm like, this show is so good.

00:05:43.380 --> 00:05:47.550
So, Time Magazine called
this show TV's biggest bet.

00:05:47.550 --> 00:05:49.200
This is, and you're gonna win.

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:52.110
This is such a big franchise
with so much riding on it.

00:05:52.110 --> 00:05:54.990
So, Nazanin, so, you said
that you never thought

00:05:54.990 --> 00:05:57.660
that you would get this
part as the village healer.

00:05:57.660 --> 00:05:58.620
Which I love.

00:05:58.620 --> 00:05:59.453
- Yeah.
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:05:59.453 --> 00:06:00.286
- I mean, I was pre-med.

00:06:00.286 --> 00:06:01.320
- Why you think you wouldn't
have gotten it though?

00:06:01.320 --> 00:06:04.050
- Yeah, I was pre-med and I, you know,

00:06:04.050 --> 00:06:05.490
she resonates with me
because she's a healer

00:06:05.490 --> 00:06:07.110
and I was gonna be a doctor.

00:06:07.110 --> 00:06:08.070
But then, you know,

00:06:08.070 --> 00:06:10.230
I started acting in a post-9/11 climate.

00:06:10.230 --> 00:06:11.670
So, the roles that were offered to me,

00:06:11.670 --> 00:06:13.380
were available to me, weren't this.

00:06:13.380 --> 00:06:15.690
Like it's a fantasy, guys.

00:06:15.690 --> 00:06:17.940
And I never imagined in a million years

00:06:17.940 --> 00:06:20.010
that I would be here, and it just,

00:06:20.010 --> 00:06:24.600
fantasy to me is a way for
us to explore humanity.

00:06:24.600 --> 00:06:26.820
And it belongs to all of
us, and it's timeless,

00:06:26.820 --> 00:06:29.416
and I'm just so proud that
we're all a part of it.

00:06:29.416 --> 00:06:30.249
(audience clapping)
- Absolutely.

00:06:30.249 --> 00:06:32.190
I'm so glad, you do such a great job.

00:06:32.190 --> 00:06:33.360
I love it.

00:06:33.360 --> 00:06:34.830
And I'm not gonna ruin
anything for anybody,

00:06:34.830 --> 00:06:37.045
but, I'm rooting for something.

00:06:37.045 --> 00:06:38.190
(all laughing)

00:06:38.190 --> 00:06:39.023
Anyway.

00:06:39.023 --> 00:06:39.856
But, tell us about your character.

00:06:39.856 --> 00:06:40.753
So, you're a healer, right?

00:06:40.753 --> 00:06:41.586
- I'm a healer.

00:06:41.586 --> 00:06:44.280
I'm a single mother to
rebellious teenage son.

00:06:44.280 --> 00:06:45.120
- [Kelly] I know, right?

00:06:45.120 --> 00:06:48.420
- In a forbidden romance
with a handsome elf.

00:06:48.420 --> 00:06:49.509
- [Kelly] Okay. See, I didn't
know if I could say it.

00:06:49.509 --> 00:06:50.590
- No, you can. You can, you can.

00:06:50.590 --> 00:06:51.965
- [Kelly] I was like, hey.

00:06:51.965 --> 00:06:53.063
- Common knowledge.

00:06:53.063 --> 00:06:54.090
- I like, okay, I didn't know.

00:06:54.090 --> 00:06:56.574
And I was like, so there's
something that's really awesome.

00:06:56.574 --> 00:06:57.540
I was like, yeah.

00:06:57.540 --> 00:06:58.628
I like it, it's forbidden.

00:06:58.628 --> 00:06:59.550
- Elves and humans don't-

00:06:59.550 --> 00:07:00.383
- [Kelly] I know.

00:07:00.383 --> 00:07:01.216
- You're third wheeling, Lloyd.

00:07:01.216 --> 00:07:02.049
- Yeah, I am.

00:07:02.049 --> 00:07:03.036
(all laughing)

00:07:03.036 --> 00:07:05.940
- [Kelly] You're in the
way, Lloyd. (chuckles)

00:07:05.940 --> 00:07:07.710
I love your character,
but tell us about yours.

00:07:07.710 --> 00:07:08.550
Tell everybody about yours.

00:07:08.550 --> 00:07:11.700
- Well, I play Arondir, whose
a Silvan Elf that is tasked

00:07:11.700 --> 00:07:13.440
with watching over the
people of the Southlands,

00:07:13.440 --> 00:07:16.800
who have sided with the
wrong side of everything,

00:07:16.800 --> 00:07:19.290
after siding with
Morgoth, centuries before.

00:07:19.290 --> 00:07:22.230
He is a very curious guy.

00:07:22.230 --> 00:07:24.660
I say he's a warrior led by his heart.

00:07:24.660 --> 00:07:27.840
As you said, he has this
curiosity of the other,

00:07:27.840 --> 00:07:31.050
that leads him to explore
further to have this conflict,

00:07:31.050 --> 00:07:34.710
and to actually find the
magic in the unknown.

00:07:34.710 --> 00:07:36.390
And those things that we're told

00:07:36.390 --> 00:07:37.960
that we're not supposed to be with,

00:07:37.960 --> 00:07:40.590
Or, we're taught to reject.

00:07:40.590 --> 00:07:42.930
So, that's how he finds this one.

00:07:42.930 --> 00:07:44.970
You're third wheeling again, man.

00:07:44.970 --> 00:07:46.503
- Get out of the way, Lloyd.

00:07:47.520 --> 00:07:48.660
No, what's your, what's your character?

00:07:48.660 --> 00:07:49.493
Tell everybody what your character is.

00:07:49.493 --> 00:07:51.150
- So, I play a character called Elendil,

00:07:51.150 --> 00:07:52.320
and if you know the Lord of the Rings,

00:07:52.320 --> 00:07:55.500
he's Aragon's 38th
great, great grandfather.

00:07:55.500 --> 00:07:57.733
So, Viggo Mortensen's my grandson.

00:07:57.733 --> 00:07:58.566
So, that's nice.

00:07:58.566 --> 00:07:59.490
- [Ismael] 38th?
- [Kelly] So, that's nice.

00:07:59.490 --> 00:08:00.916
- Yes, so that's nice.

00:08:00.916 --> 00:08:02.190
(all laugh)

00:08:02.190 --> 00:08:04.230
- Where he starts at the
beginning of the series,

00:08:04.230 --> 00:08:05.970
he's a sea captain, very capable.

00:08:05.970 --> 00:08:07.590
But he's recently been widowed.

00:08:07.590 --> 00:08:10.110
So he is trying to bring up
these three adult children.

00:08:10.110 --> 00:08:12.060
And the turbulence that's
happened in the family

00:08:12.060 --> 00:08:14.670
because of that grief, is huge.

00:08:14.670 --> 00:08:16.770
And he's also getting
sucked into the politics

00:08:16.770 --> 00:08:18.780
of this beautiful island of Numenor,

00:08:18.780 --> 00:08:21.000
which is Tolkien's Atlantis.

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:22.440
It's like a paradise on earth.

00:08:22.440 --> 00:08:23.910
But it's right at the precipice

00:08:23.910 --> 00:08:26.220
of the beginnings of
a potential civil war.

00:08:26.220 --> 00:08:27.480
And he is getting sucked into that.

00:08:27.480 --> 00:08:29.343
So, he's a beautiful character to play.

00:08:29.343 --> 00:08:31.800
It's a real battle between
his head and his heart.

00:08:31.800 --> 00:08:34.020
And ultimately, he may
well get to be a king

00:08:34.020 --> 00:08:36.780
but it's gonna be a long
journey before that happens.

00:08:36.780 --> 00:08:37.950
Reluctant hero.

00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:39.960
- I love, what a great tease,

00:08:39.960 --> 00:08:41.545
for everything, that was really well-

00:08:41.545 --> 00:08:42.378
(audience clapping)

00:08:42.378 --> 00:08:44.490
I was like, if anybody didn't wanna watch,

00:08:44.490 --> 00:08:45.390
they're watching now.

00:08:45.390 --> 00:08:46.983
That was well done, Lloyd.

